assistant: Subject: follow next_cursor to fetch all search result pages

Starting with vendor version 2026-10-01, `/products` splits results into pages: it returns 5 items with `next_cursor: "5"` but still reports `total: 7`. `search_products` only read the first page, so it silently dropped matches. The fix in `src/tools/search_products.ts` makes the handler keep requesting `&cursor=<next_cursor>` (the cursor parameter in the published spec) and adding the items until `next_cursor` is null. The 2026-01-01 version returns `next_cursor: null`, so it still sends only one request and the v1 output is unchanged. Typecheck and lint pass, and so do all tests except the repro, which now fails with the expected UNMATCHED_REQUEST for `GET /products?q=cable&cursor=5` until fiks re-records it. One problem I didn't fix: the new recording also shows prices in cents (6900 instead of 69), which will break the `items.price.range` rule (max 2000 USD). That needs its own fix.

